    "body": "Two test details from the native reproduction may help with the fix. The existing Fanuc assertion in `crates/post/tests/radius_arcs.rs` accepts an I/J fallback when a tiny arc rounds to one XY point. The new regression can distinguish that case from a true full turn.\n\nThe intermediate reader accepts fractional micrometre words. Compare the original endpoints in the active plane when deciding whether the source intended a full turn. A helical full turn can have different start and end Z values. A representable short arc, a near-full arc, and a true full turn give separate checks in inch and metric output.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
